  "title": "Kerala's Name Change Bill Passed by Lok and Rajya Sabha",
  "summary": "The Lok Sabha passed the Kerala (Alteration of Name) Bill, 2026, on August 11, 2026, followed by the Rajya Sabha the next day. The bill aims to rename the state to Keralam and has been approved by the state assembly in 2024, with the government forwarding a resolution to the Centre in June 2024.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Lok Sabha passed the Kerala (Alteration of Name) Bill, 2026, on August 11, 2026.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The state assembly passed a resolution in 2024 urging the Centre to bring a law to change the name of the state to Keralam.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bill provides for the alteration of the state's name and has been adopted by the state legislature.",
      "confidence": 0.95
